  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1965-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since the base is \\(2,\\) the exponent must be zero. Factoring gives \\[ \\begin{gathered} 2x^2-7x+5=0,\\\\ (2x-5)(x-1)=0. \\end{gathered} \\] Thus \\(x=\\frac{5}{2}\\) or \\(x=1,\\) giving two real values.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "A positive base other than \\(1\\) has value \\(1\\) only at exponent \\(0\\)",
        "Solve \\(2x^2-7x+5=0\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
